1
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:11,880
No breathing or pulse.

2
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:12,880
Prepare for CPR.

3
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:14,400
- Prepare the AED. - Copy that.

4
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:16,960
The AED is ready.

5
00:01:18,640 --> 00:01:20,040
Stand back from the patient. Prepare for shock.

6
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:21,120
Clear.

7
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:22,920
Pack up. Prepare to board the ambulance.

8
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:39,720
Let's go.

9
00:03:05,200 --> 00:03:07,520
Ms. Yau, are you okay?

10
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:12,720
It was just a dream.

11
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:16,280
It's not real.

12
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:56,920
Stop it.

13
00:04:58,920 --> 00:04:59,920
Sit down.

14
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:17,560
I am now officially hiring you...

15
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:18,840
to be my legal representative.

16
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:57,600
(Episode 1)

17
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,480
(This is a work of fiction.)

18
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:02,320
(Three Days Ago)

19
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:03,320
Mr. Lo,

20
00:07:03,720 --> 00:07:06,840
on July 27, 2020,

21
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,960
did you attend the "Boat P"...

22
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:12,240
hosted by Lee Tze Yan at Hebe Haven, Sai Kung,

23
00:07:12,320 --> 00:07:14,120
as in a yacht party?

24
00:07:14,920 --> 00:07:15,960
Yes.

25
00:07:15,960 --> 00:07:17,760
According to Lee Tze Yan's testimony,

26
00:07:18,400 --> 00:07:20,280
this yacht party was actually a sex party.

27
00:07:21,200 --> 00:07:22,840
As long as guests paid to board,

28
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:25,320
they could have sex...

29
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:26,600
with anyone on the yacht.

30
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,400
You were a waiter on the yacht at the time,

31
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:33,120
and you had sex with Mr. Chiu Wing Tai.

32
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,320
- Do you agree? - I do.

33
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:40,840
Was that the first time you met Chiu Wing Tai?

34
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:43,000
- Yes. - Here is my understanding.

35
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:46,400
Your relationship began with a sexual transaction.

36
00:07:46,480 --> 00:07:48,360
- Do you agree? - I disagree.

37
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:51,000
There was no money involved between us.

38
00:07:51,520 --> 00:07:53,320
I liked him, so I slept with him.

39
00:07:53,760 --> 00:07:55,040
We started dating after that.

40
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:56,800
We were truly in love.

41
00:07:57,760 --> 00:08:01,960
Please open the bundle in front of you to page 14.

42
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:07,200
This is Mr. Chiu Wing Tai's ledger.

43
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:10,200
Starting from July 27, 2020,

44
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:12,280
the year he met you,

45
00:08:13,160 --> 00:08:15,680
there are entries marked "Entertainment".

46
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:18,000
They range from a few thousand dollars...

47
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,800
to tens of thousands,

48
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,480
and eventually hundreds of thousands.

49
00:08:25,320 --> 00:08:28,200
Page 16 shows your bank deposit records.

50
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,760
The amounts in both records match.

51
00:08:33,200 --> 00:08:34,440
Do you agree?

52
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:38,240
I do.

53
00:08:38,680 --> 00:08:41,520
That means the transactional sex between you two continued...

54
00:08:42,040 --> 00:08:43,120
until his death?

55
00:08:43,520 --> 00:08:45,520
I told you, it wasn't transactional sex.

56
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:46,520
Those were living expenses.

57
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:48,960
He loved me and wanted to take care of me, so he gave me money.

58
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:50,760
He wrote "Entertainment" in his ledger...

59
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,560
just because he didn't want his wife to know.

60
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:57,440
So you insist that it was because he loved you...

61
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,440
that he gave you money, right?

62
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:00,800
Of course.

63
00:09:03,560 --> 00:09:07,000
Please turn to page 28 of the document bundle.

64
00:09:09,760 --> 00:09:11,640
(The Third-Generation Successor of the Nuen Lap Brand)

65
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,680
(Family Heirloom Cloth Passed Down for a Hundred Years)

66
00:09:13,280 --> 00:09:14,800
What do you see in the photo?

67
00:09:16,640 --> 00:09:17,640
Tai and his wife.

68
00:09:18,680 --> 00:09:20,520
Apart from them, what else is there?

69
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:25,960
Their "family heirloom cloth".

70
00:09:27,200 --> 00:09:30,320
You said you were Chiu Wing Tai's true love.

71
00:09:30,400 --> 00:09:34,000
But he never mentioned this cloth to you.

72
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,680
He did.

73
00:09:37,480 --> 00:09:39,760
He said it was the first piece of fabric his grandfather wove...

74
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:41,040
after founding the Nuen Lap brand.

75
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:44,880
But you didn't mention this cloth at all...

76
00:09:44,960 --> 00:09:46,200
in your witness statement.

77
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:49,120
You only found out about its existence...

78
00:09:49,200 --> 00:09:51,600
after reading the statement...

79
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:54,040
of the defendant, Ms. Chan Shuk Ching.

80
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:56,320
Do you agree?

81
00:09:59,160 --> 00:10:00,160
Tai said so many things to me.

82
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,360
How could I remember them all?

83
00:10:04,480 --> 00:10:05,480
Exactly.

84
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:08,480
People usually only remember the most important things.

85
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:10,400
Chiu Wing Tai...

86
00:10:11,120 --> 00:10:13,880
Three generations of his family have taken photos with this cloth.

87
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,440
Look at page five.

88
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:21,400
Chiu Wing Tai said in a press interview...

89
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,320
that this cloth was very important to him.

90
00:10:24,640 --> 00:10:26,000
In fact, it was the most important thing.

91
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:28,960
When he first met his wife,

92
00:10:29,040 --> 00:10:30,800
he even let her touch this cloth.

93
00:10:30,920 --> 00:10:32,040
He even said...

94
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:34,000
that before he died,

95
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:37,320
he would give it to the person he loved most.

96
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,640
If you were really Chiu Wing Tai's true love,

97
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,400
why wouldn't you remember...

98
00:10:42,480 --> 00:10:44,760
how much this cloth meant to him?

99
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:47,160
If he really loved you that much,

100
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,680
why didn't he mention in his will...

101
00:10:49,760 --> 00:10:51,240
that he was leaving this cloth to you?

102
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,320
It's precisely because...

103
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:57,000
your relationship was just a sexual transaction.

104
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:00,760
Tell me, why would a normal person...

105
00:11:00,840 --> 00:11:02,600
leave their entire estate...

106
00:11:02,680 --> 00:11:04,600
to a paid sexual partner?

107
00:11:07,160 --> 00:11:08,440
Therefore, this will is a forgery.

108
00:11:09,360 --> 00:11:12,560
Chiu Wing Tai never intended to leave his estate to you.

109
00:11:12,840 --> 00:11:13,840
Do you agree?

110
00:11:14,320 --> 00:11:16,960
That's not true. He loved me!

111
00:11:17,120 --> 00:11:19,400
You can't say he didn't love me just because of a piece of cloth!

112
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,240
You didn't know him at all!

113
00:11:21,320 --> 00:11:23,200
Plaintiff, please remain calm.

114
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,600
Please control your emotions.

115
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,280
- Everyone, stay calm. - Should an ambulance be called?

116
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,120
Due to the plaintiff's condition,

117
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:33,960
this trial is now adjourned.

118
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:38,520
I told the judge you're still unwell.

119
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,080
She has adjourned the case for three days.

120
00:11:42,120 --> 00:11:43,480
That was a good move back there.

121
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:45,440
You should've gained a lot of sympathy.

122
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,200
I can't believe you didn't know about that rag.

123
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,520
You let them question me like a fool.

124
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:51,560
I warned you. I told you to rehearse.

125
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,760
I paid you to handle everything for me.

126
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,120
And now you're blaming me?

127
00:11:57,520 --> 00:11:58,520
Get out.

128
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:00,320
Get lost!

129
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,800
I have another candidate in mind.

130
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:16,640
But her fees are very high.

131
00:12:17,640 --> 00:12:18,640
Is she a guaranteed win?

132
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,560
The reason her fees are so high...

133
00:12:22,080 --> 00:12:24,280
is because she'll do anything to win.

134
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:29,360
Our bonus is coming!

135
00:12:29,440 --> 00:12:30,480
Counselor Yau?

136
00:12:30,720 --> 00:12:31,720
What is it?

137
00:12:31,800 --> 00:12:34,080
One visit from her covers the whole shop's bonuses for months.

138
00:12:57,080 --> 00:12:58,080
Let's look at the bags first.

139
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:01,000
Counselor Yau, this is our new...

140
00:13:03,760 --> 00:13:05,960
This is a special edition Baguette.

141
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,200
Each crystal was hand-set...

142
00:13:08,280 --> 00:13:10,360
- Wrap it up. - Thank you, Counselor Yau.

143
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:13,200
- This one... - Didn't I buy this in black?

144
00:13:13,280 --> 00:13:16,040
This one is hand-woven in genuine leather.

145
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,560
- There are only 10 in the world. - Wrap it up.

146
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:41,560
Go to Blue Box and get me a coffee.

147
00:13:43,880 --> 00:13:44,880
Why isn't the door closed?

148
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:04,320
(Counselor Yau Yam Yam)

149
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:10,680
Another razor blade?

150
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,560
So unoriginal. How many is that this month?

151
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:15,160
You've got me there.

152
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,200
(Die)

153
00:14:18,360 --> 00:14:19,760
How colorful.

154
00:14:21,920 --> 00:14:22,920
Hello, Officer Chow.

155
00:14:22,920 --> 00:14:24,640
It's Bionca, Counselor Yau's secretary.

156
00:14:25,240 --> 00:14:27,000
Yes, another razor blade in the mail.

157
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:35,480
- Counselor Yau. - Counselor Yau.

158
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,320
What do we have?

159
00:14:56,600 --> 00:14:57,920
One is the owner of Ngan Fai Restaurant...

160
00:14:57,920 --> 00:14:58,960
getting a divorce.

161
00:14:59,040 --> 00:15:00,320
He wants to split the assets with his wife.

162
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,720
Another is a retired superintendent...

163
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:02,960
who wants to sue his friend for defamation.

164
00:15:03,120 --> 00:15:04,880
And this one is currently in court.

165
00:15:04,960 --> 00:15:06,200
The inheritance case of the owner of Nuen Lap.

166
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,280
He wants to change his barrister.

167
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:10,560
Handle the Nuen Lap case first.

168
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:19,000
I'm sorry, I won't take it.

169
00:15:22,160 --> 00:15:23,160
Why?

170
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,120
Even though Gordon and I are friends,

171
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,640
he took the wrong approach from the start.

172
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,440
It's basically a lost cause.

173
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,000
If I were to take over,

174
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,960
I would have to come up with all new tactics.

175
00:15:34,320 --> 00:15:35,880
First, there might not be enough time.

176
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:38,040
Second, taking over near the end,

177
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,760
the legal fees I would earn would be limited.

178
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,320
I don't think it's worth it.

179
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:47,800
Name your price.

180
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:51,320
Just a routine reminder.

181
00:15:51,760 --> 00:15:53,360
Discussing fees like this...

182
00:15:53,440 --> 00:15:54,720
is actually against the rules.

183
00:15:54,800 --> 00:15:56,400
You see all those people waiting outside?

184
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,160
Even if you pay double,

185
00:15:59,920 --> 00:16:01,960
it's less than what I would make from a new case.

186
00:16:03,440 --> 00:16:04,440
I'm sorry.

187
00:16:06,160 --> 00:16:07,320
Show Mr. Lo out.

188
00:16:09,840 --> 00:16:12,440
This is the total value of Chiu Wing Tai's estate.

189
00:16:13,200 --> 00:16:14,560
If you can win the case,

190
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,600
I'll give you three percent.

191
00:16:35,320 --> 00:16:36,520
Then you'll have to tell me...

192
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:38,800
what you and Chiu Wing Tai ate every day,

193
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:40,440
where you went, your text messages,

194
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:41,560
and how often you had sex.

195
00:16:41,640 --> 00:16:44,480
I need to know every private detail.

196
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,240
Regarding Jeffrey's will,

197
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:51,480
both witnesses are not in Hong Kong.

198
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:54,200
Plus, Judge To is famously conservative.

199
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,680
It's really not looking good.

200
00:16:55,760 --> 00:16:57,040
Tell me something useful.

201
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:04,600
I just want to ensure my husband's wishes...

202
00:17:05,160 --> 00:17:06,240
are not being distorted.

203
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,200
If he truly wanted to leave his estate...

204
00:17:09,280 --> 00:17:10,640
to this young man,

205
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,360
I would accept it.

206
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:17,680
But as I understand it, he was misled.

207
00:17:18,680 --> 00:17:19,680
What's the wife's background?

208
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:22,600
Mrs. Chiu is very low-key. There's not much info.

209
00:17:22,880 --> 00:17:25,040
She married Chiu Wing Tai at 20...

210
00:17:25,040 --> 00:17:26,560
and has been a devoted wife and mother.

211
00:17:26,640 --> 00:17:28,280
She usually does charity work.

212
00:17:40,560 --> 00:17:42,240
I'm looking at the videos on Jeffrey's phone.

213
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:51,040
The whole folder is full of them, dozens of videos.

214
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,600
You're not recording this, are you?

215
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:57,040
I didn't agree to let you film.

216
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,000
What's wrong?

217
00:17:59,240 --> 00:18:00,840
I want to watch it later.

218
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:02,360
What if it leaks?

219
00:18:02,360 --> 00:18:04,720
We had a deal. No photos or videos.

220
00:18:05,040 --> 00:18:06,720
Okay, just this once.

221
00:18:06,800 --> 00:18:07,960
Don't be mad, okay?

222
00:18:08,480 --> 00:18:09,480
Delete it now.

223
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,680
Don't worry, I'm very careful.

224
00:18:11,760 --> 00:18:12,800
I won't let anyone know.

225
00:18:13,240 --> 00:18:15,200
If you don't delete it, get out now.

226
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:17,360
Okay, I'll delete it right now.

227
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:21,400
It's deleted.

228
00:18:21,720 --> 00:18:23,160
- Is that true? - Yes.

229
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:25,080
Stop being naughty.

230
00:18:25,960 --> 00:18:27,640
Do you think...

231
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:30,520
Jeffrey used these videos to...

232
00:18:32,520 --> 00:18:33,520
They could be useful.

233
00:18:34,200 --> 00:18:35,560
How can we present secretly filmed videos in court?

234
00:18:36,680 --> 00:18:38,800
Being useful doesn't necessarily mean presenting them in court.

235
00:18:48,160 --> 00:18:50,320
The company finally turned a profit this quarter.

236
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,320
I haven't been this happy in a long time.

237
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:53,440
Come and keep me company.

238
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,080
I thought of some new tricks today.

239
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:57,320
Say it and we'll do it.

240
00:18:59,560 --> 00:19:00,920
I'm only going to say this once.

241
00:19:01,320 --> 00:19:03,400
I love you, okay?

242
00:19:03,480 --> 00:19:05,400
Transcribe all the dialogue from the audio files for me.

243
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,000
Hello, Senior.

244
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,240
Do something for me.

245
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:22,520
Today is the first day of the trial...

246
00:19:22,600 --> 00:19:23,600
for the estate of famous movie star Shek Chung.

247
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,840
This case has caught the city's attention.

248
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,400
Shek Chung's wife, Kwok Miu Wah,

249
00:19:28,480 --> 00:19:30,920
is challenging the validity of the will.

250
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:33,640
The defendant is their only son, Shek Kwong Sing.

251
00:19:33,720 --> 00:19:35,400
Mother and son will face off in court.

252
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,840
I brought my father-in-law here today.

253
00:19:38,560 --> 00:19:40,200
I hope he is watching in the afterlife...

254
00:19:41,520 --> 00:19:42,520
and will bless us...

255
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:44,120
and support us.

256
00:19:51,960 --> 00:19:53,160
Taking on such a tough case...

257
00:19:53,520 --> 00:19:54,680
Are you that desperate for money?

258
00:19:56,600 --> 00:19:57,920
My opponent is just you.

259
00:19:57,920 --> 00:20:00,000
It's easy money. Why wouldn't I take it?

260
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,160
Master.

261
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,720
I have something to ask you.

262
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,560
You guys go in first.

263
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:34,920
How about tonight?

264
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:37,360
Sorry, my wife is sick.

265
00:20:38,040 --> 00:20:39,200
Okay, no problem.

266
00:20:39,720 --> 00:20:41,560
Happy birthday. I'll make it up to you.

267
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,200
I'll go in first.

268
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:51,880
Court.

269
00:21:10,440 --> 00:21:11,440
Counselor Yau.

270
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:14,920
Please take off your earrings.

271
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,000
They're too bright.

272
00:21:23,360 --> 00:21:24,840
No problem, Your Honor.

273
00:21:32,480 --> 00:21:33,960
You've been married for 45 years.

274
00:21:34,560 --> 00:21:36,160
Was it only because of this lawsuit...

275
00:21:36,560 --> 00:21:39,480
and the appearance of the plaintiff, Mr. Lo Ho Chun,

276
00:21:39,920 --> 00:21:43,040
that you realized your husband liked men?

277
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,920
I don't think he liked men.

278
00:21:47,520 --> 00:21:49,160
He was just looking for something new.

279
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:52,000
Does that mean yes or no?

280
00:21:52,800 --> 00:21:55,160
No, he didn't like men.

281
00:21:55,240 --> 00:21:57,320
Then do you think your husband loved you?

282
00:21:58,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Yes.

283
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,920
When was the last time he told you he loved you...

284
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:03,360
or was intimate with you?

285
00:22:07,240 --> 00:22:08,680
Witness, please answer the question.

286
00:22:10,360 --> 00:22:12,600
I don't keep track of things like that.

287
00:22:12,680 --> 00:22:13,680
You don't?

288
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:17,040
Is it because it's been so long...

289
00:22:17,040 --> 00:22:18,080
that you can't remember?

290
00:22:18,080 --> 00:22:19,080
Objection.

291
00:22:19,840 --> 00:22:22,240
The question is speculative and irrelevant.

292
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:24,840
Objection sustained. The witness doesn't need to answer.

293
00:22:25,400 --> 00:22:26,400
Your Honor,

294
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,800
I have no further questions.

295
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:31,280
Dr. Fong,

296
00:22:31,280 --> 00:22:33,320
what was Chiu Wing Tai's physical condition...

297
00:22:33,320 --> 00:22:34,760
in his final two months?

298
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:37,480
He needed long-term blood pressure meds...

299
00:22:37,560 --> 00:22:39,680
and a targeted drug for liver cancer.

300
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:43,000
If he didn't take his blood pressure meds regularly,

301
00:22:43,680 --> 00:22:44,680
what would happen?

302
00:22:45,320 --> 00:22:47,840
He might have a rapid heart rate, blurred vision,

303
00:22:47,840 --> 00:22:50,760
confusion, headaches, and weakness.

304
00:22:51,080 --> 00:22:54,920
Would this also affect the patient's judgment?

305
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,480
Yes.

306
00:22:57,440 --> 00:23:00,240
You went to Chiu Wing Tai's villa...

307
00:23:00,320 --> 00:23:01,320
to treat him.

308
00:23:01,560 --> 00:23:03,520
Who was taking care of him then?

309
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,360
It was Mr. Lo Ho Chun.

310
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:09,160
Do you think it's possible...

311
00:23:09,160 --> 00:23:10,360
that Mr. Lo Ho Chun forgot...

312
00:23:10,360 --> 00:23:11,960
to give Chiu Wing Tai his medication,

313
00:23:12,360 --> 00:23:15,000
thereby impairing his judgment?

314
00:23:17,120 --> 00:23:18,120
That is possible.

315
00:23:18,720 --> 00:23:19,720
I have no further questions.

316
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,200
Counselor Yau.

317
00:23:23,120 --> 00:23:25,480
Your Honor, the plaintiff has no cross-examination.

318
00:23:26,960 --> 00:23:29,960
The defense may call the next witness.

319
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:34,320
We compared over 40 signatures...

320
00:23:34,320 --> 00:23:36,960
from Mr. Chiu's daily documents.

321
00:23:37,400 --> 00:23:39,800
They match the handwriting on the will.

322
00:23:40,040 --> 00:23:43,040
However, the strokes on the will's signature...

323
00:23:43,400 --> 00:23:44,800
are clearly more forceful than usual.

324
00:23:45,080 --> 00:23:46,920
This indicates he was...

325
00:23:46,920 --> 00:23:48,760
in an intense emotional state.

326
00:23:49,400 --> 00:23:53,000
Could you elaborate on what kind of intense emotion?

327
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:56,080
He might have been feeling very angry,

328
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:57,640
highly agitated,

329
00:23:57,920 --> 00:23:59,560
or perhaps he was even unwilling to sign.

330
00:24:00,040 --> 00:24:01,360
No further questions, Your Honor.

331
00:24:03,720 --> 00:24:04,720
Counselor Yau.

332
00:24:06,760 --> 00:24:07,760
Your Honor,

333
00:24:08,200 --> 00:24:09,400
the plaintiff has no cross-examination.

334
00:24:42,920 --> 00:24:44,440
Court is adjourned. We will resume this afternoon.

335
00:24:44,800 --> 00:24:45,960
Court.

336
00:25:06,120 --> 00:25:07,160
I'm going to the restroom.

337
00:25:36,360 --> 00:25:37,360
You left your phone.

338
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,920
It's not mine.

339
00:25:40,280 --> 00:25:41,440
Not yours?

340
00:25:42,880 --> 00:25:45,600
It has videos of your husband. It should be yours.

341
00:25:54,280 --> 00:25:55,280
You said...

342
00:25:55,800 --> 00:25:57,400
if this was your husband's last wish,

343
00:25:57,400 --> 00:25:58,520
you would fulfill it.

344
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,480
These videos don't mean anything.

345
00:26:04,560 --> 00:26:07,200
He loved me. He wouldn't do this to me.

346
00:26:07,280 --> 00:26:08,840
He wouldn't leave me with nothing.

347
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,840
Sleeping together might not mean anything.

348
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:14,320
But being together for over 40 years...

349
00:26:14,800 --> 00:26:16,120
might not mean anything either.

350
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,280
Perhaps to him,

351
00:26:19,280 --> 00:26:20,920
those 40-odd years were just a duty.

352
00:26:20,920 --> 00:26:22,440
And for the sake of that duty,

353
00:26:23,240 --> 00:26:24,600
he turned his entire life...

354
00:26:24,600 --> 00:26:25,640
into a lie.

355
00:26:26,960 --> 00:26:28,440
Only during this past year with Jeffrey...

356
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,920
could he truly be himself.

357
00:26:32,760 --> 00:26:33,760
Look.

358
00:26:36,080 --> 00:26:38,640
Who do you think he was happier with?

359
00:26:39,240 --> 00:26:40,240
Then say you love me.

360
00:26:42,880 --> 00:26:45,640
You can't approach me privately. I'll report you.

361
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:47,800
I love you.

362
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,240
I've never been this happy.

363
00:26:50,920 --> 00:26:52,200
If only every day could be like this.

364
00:26:52,680 --> 00:26:53,680
You can come see me every day.

365
00:26:53,680 --> 00:26:54,720
How long has it been...

366
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:57,320
since he said those things to you?

367
00:26:57,720 --> 00:26:59,240
It's not too late.

368
00:26:59,240 --> 00:27:01,320
She's always nagging me at home.

369
00:27:02,200 --> 00:27:04,600
I only found out about these videos...

370
00:27:04,600 --> 00:27:05,760
after I took over this case.

371
00:27:07,080 --> 00:27:08,840
Jeffrey didn't want to make them public.

372
00:27:08,840 --> 00:27:10,200
He wanted to protect your husband.

373
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,440
But I feel that...

374
00:27:12,440 --> 00:27:14,560
these are vital proof of their love.

375
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,680
I'm showing them to you now...

376
00:27:18,080 --> 00:27:20,760
out of respect for you and your husband.

377
00:27:22,480 --> 00:27:23,960
I hope we can reach a settlement.

378
00:27:24,760 --> 00:27:25,960
Let's not let things get ugly.

379
00:27:32,880 --> 00:27:34,200
I can tell you...

380
00:27:35,240 --> 00:27:36,440
that they have many of these videos.

381
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:39,880
They were all filmed consensually.

382
00:27:40,840 --> 00:27:41,880
They're very sweet.

383
00:27:43,160 --> 00:27:44,240
And it's clear...

384
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,080
that they really loved each other.

385
00:27:49,680 --> 00:27:50,720
So...

386
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:54,600
if you won't fulfill your husband's wish,

387
00:27:56,760 --> 00:27:59,760
I'll release these videos for his sake.

388
00:28:03,040 --> 00:28:06,440
You'll have to see if you can handle that.

389
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,720
I have a settlement proposal.

390
00:28:18,160 --> 00:28:20,280
It will definitely protect your current quality of life.

391
00:28:24,240 --> 00:28:26,600
I know you're not greedy for money.

392
00:28:27,560 --> 00:28:28,960
You just want an answer.

393
00:28:30,960 --> 00:28:32,200
And the answer is...

394
00:28:34,600 --> 00:28:37,800
your husband really loved Jeffrey.

395
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,000
Since he couldn't give him a status,

396
00:28:42,080 --> 00:28:43,320
he could only leave him an inheritance.

397
00:28:45,720 --> 00:28:47,560
I know this truth is hard to accept,

398
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:51,640
but it was indeed your husband's wish.

399
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:05,360
You would want him to rest in peace, right?

400
00:29:08,440 --> 00:29:09,720
If you really loved him,

401
00:29:11,600 --> 00:29:12,640
you should respect his choice.

402
00:29:31,720 --> 00:29:32,720
Court.

403
00:29:44,760 --> 00:29:45,960
What is it, Counselor Ma?

404
00:29:48,080 --> 00:29:49,080
Your Honor,

405
00:29:49,840 --> 00:29:53,720
my client has reached a settlement with the plaintiff.

406
00:29:55,080 --> 00:29:57,760
This is the draft of the court order...

407
00:29:58,200 --> 00:29:59,880
jointly prepared by both parties.

408
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:14,920
Why the sudden settlement?

409
00:30:15,440 --> 00:30:16,440
What is the reason?

410
00:30:18,320 --> 00:30:19,920
My client has had a change of heart.

411
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:22,480
She believes her late husband's wish...

412
00:30:22,560 --> 00:30:24,960
was to leave the estate to the plaintiff.

413
00:30:25,440 --> 00:30:26,440
Counselor Ma,

414
00:30:26,880 --> 00:30:29,360
you have a responsibility to act...

415
00:30:29,360 --> 00:30:30,800
in your client's best interest.

416
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:34,040
Have you explained the situation clearly to her?

417
00:30:35,440 --> 00:30:38,640
Yes, but she still decided to settle.

418
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:48,720
If that's the case,

419
00:30:49,360 --> 00:30:51,320
the court is pleased to see a settlement reached.

420
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:53,720
I hope both parties are satisfied with this outcome.

421
00:30:54,400 --> 00:30:55,400
Court is adjourned.

422
00:30:55,720 --> 00:30:56,720
Court.

423
00:31:09,960 --> 00:31:11,560
What exactly did you do?

424
00:31:12,560 --> 00:31:14,600
I fought for my client's best interest.

425
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:30,520
I really did...

426
00:31:30,760 --> 00:31:31,920
force him to sign that will.

427
00:31:38,640 --> 00:31:40,320
- What did you tell her? - Nothing.

428
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:50,000
You! Stop right there!

429
00:31:53,680 --> 00:31:54,960
Were you lying to me just now?

430
00:31:56,000 --> 00:31:58,480
That jerk said he forced my husband to sign it!

431
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:02,920
You lied to me.

432
00:32:03,520 --> 00:32:04,960
I'm going to report you for harassment!

433
00:32:05,600 --> 00:32:06,600
I'm going to appeal!

434
00:32:19,240 --> 00:32:20,880
I didn't hold a gun to your head to make you settle.

435
00:32:22,800 --> 00:32:23,800
You believed me...

436
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:26,120
because you know very well...

437
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:28,200
that your husband didn't love you at all.

438
00:32:43,920 --> 00:32:44,960
You jerk!

439
00:32:46,000 --> 00:32:47,440
Karma will get you both!

440
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,160
You'll be struck by lightning!

441
00:32:49,240 --> 00:32:50,840
You'll suffer in your final years!

442
00:32:58,280 --> 00:33:00,080
500 million.

443
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,240
Have you ever seen 500 million dollars?

444
00:33:01,240 --> 00:33:02,240
500 million!

445
00:33:02,240 --> 00:33:03,400
What exactly did you do to that woman?

446
00:33:04,320 --> 00:33:05,320
You don't need to know.

447
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:09,600
You're worth every penny.

448
00:33:11,960 --> 00:33:13,720
I'm having a party tonight. You guys should come.

449
00:33:14,160 --> 00:33:15,520
No, thanks, we have things to do.

450
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:16,960
Have fun.

451
00:33:38,680 --> 00:33:40,200
I feel a bit sorry for Mrs. Chiu.

452
00:33:42,840 --> 00:33:45,440
Sex clips and homosexuality...

453
00:33:46,000 --> 00:33:47,040
are quite common nowadays.

454
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,760
People would have forgotten in a few days.

455
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:52,680
If she had taken that mindset, she wouldn't have lost so much.

456
00:33:53,840 --> 00:33:56,160
She just wanted to respect her husband's wishes.

457
00:33:58,200 --> 00:33:59,600
When her husband was cheating on her,

458
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:01,400
did he ever respect her?

459
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:04,640
The man is dead.

460
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:06,320
Who cares about his wishes?

461
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,160
She's even more of a fool,

462
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:11,480
giving up hundreds of millions for someone who didn't love her.

463
00:34:14,680 --> 00:34:15,840
Feelings are all fake.

464
00:34:16,840 --> 00:34:18,040
The most important thing is to look out for yourself.

465
00:34:19,240 --> 00:34:21,080
The living can deceive you.

466
00:34:21,280 --> 00:34:23,560
The dead can be used to deceive you too.

467
00:34:24,600 --> 00:34:25,600
You must remember,

468
00:34:26,400 --> 00:34:28,760
people are the most untrustworthy.

469
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:34,360
When you get married, remember to sign a prenup.

470
00:34:35,440 --> 00:34:36,480
Money...

471
00:34:37,440 --> 00:34:41,440
is your only friend, husband, and parent.

472
00:34:59,360 --> 00:35:00,360
Master.

473
00:35:04,120 --> 00:35:06,840
It's my dating anniversary today.

474
00:35:07,200 --> 00:35:08,240
Can I leave early?

475
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:11,440
As long as the case files are on my desk...

476
00:35:11,640 --> 00:35:13,280
before we start work tomorrow.

477
00:35:15,560 --> 00:35:17,480
Then I'll come back after dinner.

478
00:35:38,680 --> 00:35:40,800
(Master)

479
00:35:40,800 --> 00:35:43,160
(Are you free tonight?)

480
00:35:43,240 --> 00:35:45,320
(Master: Any update?)

481
00:35:45,320 --> 00:35:47,240
(Find you now.)

482
00:35:47,320 --> 00:35:50,880
(Can I meet you for a while?)

483
00:35:50,880 --> 00:35:51,880
(Ben: Driving over now. Wait for me.)

484
00:35:51,880 --> 00:35:52,880
(Are you free tonight?)

485
00:35:52,880 --> 00:35:53,880
(Ben: Be right there. The usual place?)

486
00:35:53,880 --> 00:35:54,880
(Yes.)

487
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:56,000
(Ben: I'm here. Where are you?)

488
00:35:56,000 --> 00:35:59,560
(Are you free tonight?)

489
00:36:00,040 --> 00:36:01,960
At your beck and call. Happy birthday.

490
00:36:23,480 --> 00:36:24,480
Happy birthday.

491
00:36:40,320 --> 00:36:41,320
Make a wish first.

492
00:36:53,840 --> 00:36:54,840
Which one do you want?

493
00:36:55,160 --> 00:36:57,320
There's Moneybag Cat and Piggy Cat.

494
00:36:59,920 --> 00:37:00,920
It's the one!

495
00:37:04,480 --> 00:37:05,840
It's okay. We have five more boxes.

496
00:37:05,840 --> 00:37:06,840
Open the others first.

497
00:37:08,720 --> 00:37:09,720
It doesn't matter.

498
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:11,560
Duplicates are more fun. One for each of us.

499
00:37:13,960 --> 00:37:14,960
The last one.

500
00:37:16,880 --> 00:37:19,360
I have a feeling it's the Diamond Cat. Go for it.

501
00:37:20,320 --> 00:37:25,880
Diamond Cat.

502
00:37:26,720 --> 00:37:29,520
Diamond Cat.

503
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:38,200
We couldn't complete the set.

504
00:37:38,280 --> 00:37:41,000
It's okay. We have four pairs of twins.

505
00:37:41,720 --> 00:37:43,080
That's even harder than a full set.

506
00:37:45,960 --> 00:37:46,960
Wait for me.

507
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:59,120
You're all new members of my family now.

508
00:38:07,040 --> 00:38:08,040
A full set.

509
00:38:10,080 --> 00:38:11,120
How did you get that?

510
00:38:36,800 --> 00:38:38,440
The cake is here.

511
00:38:40,520 --> 00:38:41,880
Happy birthday.

512
00:38:42,280 --> 00:38:44,640
This is the last time we're visiting you.

513
00:38:45,560 --> 00:38:48,200
Don't wish to see us anymore.

514
00:38:48,680 --> 00:38:50,120
It's a waste of a birthday wish.

515
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:52,640
I hope you'll be happy from now on.

516
00:38:53,280 --> 00:38:54,840
Truly happy.

517
00:38:55,520 --> 00:38:58,280
Only if you're happy can we leave in peace.

518
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:04,360
Grandpa, Grandma!

519
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:37,200
It's your birthday. No need.

520
00:39:37,960 --> 00:39:40,120
Let me teach you something. Don't do business at a loss.

521
00:39:40,560 --> 00:39:42,240
Seeing you is worth it already.

522
00:39:43,320 --> 00:39:45,920
Hey.

523
00:41:49,320 --> 00:41:50,320
Are you okay?

524
00:41:53,360 --> 00:41:54,360
I...

525
00:41:55,520 --> 00:41:56,520
I'm calling the police.
